    <h1>About</h1>
    <p>
      I'm Stefanus Hinardi, a software engineer based in Seattle.
    </p>
    <p>
      I studied Computer Science at the University of Illinois at Urbana-Champaign and received
      my Master's in Electrical Engineering and Computer Science from UC Berkeley.
    </p>
    <p>
      Outside of work, I enjoy writing, photography, travel, and reading — particularly
      literature from Southeast Asia and East Asia.
    </p>
    <p>
      This blog is called <em>Aksara</em>, which means "letter" or "script" in Indonesian and
      several other Southeast Asian languages.
    </p>
